  "id": "COMPOUND:21269 - PROTEIN:813",
  "verbalization": "The compound [(1'R,2S,2'R,3'R,5'S,8'R,9'R,10'R,13'S)-2',9',13'-triacetyloxy-10'-hydroxy-8',12',15',15'-tetramethylspiro[oxirane-2,4'-tricyclo[9.3.1.03,8]pentadec-11-ene]-5'-yl] (3R)-3-(dimethylamino)-3-phenylpropanoate) is consistently identified as a target of the Kappa-type opioid receptor through multiple pathways. It is directly linked to the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, which in turn is targeted by several compounds, including Ginkgolide A and 3-Methylfentanyl. These findings suggest a potential mechanism where the compound may interact with the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, which is known to be a target of Kappa-type opioid receptors. The evidence supports a possible role for this compound in modulating the Kappa-type opioid receptor through interactions with the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, highlighting a complex network of receptor targets that may be influenced by the compound's pharmacological profile.",
